Kim Hunter wrote:
> 
> Is there a way to set up the console on a Vaxstation 3100 M38 to go to
> one of the serial ports vice the normal worstation monitor?

Yes, the Owner's manual details how to perform this operation (p. A-4). 
I'll assume that you don't have access to the manual, so I'll summarize
from the written description:

With the system turned off, find the S3 icon over the alternate console
slide-switch on the back of the system unit.  Down is the normal
position.  Set the alternate console switch to the up position, making
the serial (printer) port a terminal port.  You'll need to set the baud
rate on the alternate console terminal to 9600.  Power on your system,
and look for the console prompt (>>>) on the alternate console.  The S3
switch is only read at system power-up, so the hard power-off is
necessary.
