Kim Hunter wrote:
> 
> I have been away from the VMS groups for awhile. I will be making use of
> my VMS box as a web and smtp/pop mail server. Is the osu web server
> still the best server around for VMS. What about smtp/pop - I heard MX
> was pretty good. Any feedback?
> 
> Thanks in advance.
> 
> Ken :)

OSU is a very good web server, and it's free.  As for SMTP/POP, MX does
not have a POP server.  All of the TCP/IP stacks for VMS (TCPware,
Multinet, Attachemate, and UCX) come with SMTP and POP servers.  The
next release of TCPware will also include an IMAP server.

