Either use any of the TCP/IP stacks that come with a POP server, as Mr. Levy
pointed out, or use IUPOP3 (actually, the UCX POP3 server is based on it).

Get it from ftp.indiana.edu in /pub/vms/iupop3 , and (for v1.8 - not sure
whether these changes made it into the latest version (1.9?)) patch it:

1. according to http://www.tci.uni-hannover.de/extrakt/pop.html
   to get UIDL to work
   (optional POP3 command, activated by e.g. "leave mail on server" in Netscape)

2. to cover MIME, compile with IGNORE_MAIL11_HEADERS #define'd, and with
   the changes described below

